{{!-- /the-faith-received/guide/ — one guide per shelf at ?s=<shelf>, and
     without ?s= the guides themselves with a century ruler over every
     shelf (the owner, 2026-10-10: "from browse the shelves it can be quick
     to find a time, but clicking into it it could be its own explainer with
     graphic motion and everything").

     One template for all of them, the pattern of the tradition pages.
     assets/js/faith-guide.js reads ?s=, fetches that shelf's markup and
     data from assets/data/faith-received/guides/, and runs its scenes
     (assets/js/faith-guide-<shelf>.js) on the shared engine
     (assets/js/faith-guide-engine.js). The motion is GSAP with its
     ScrollTrigger, and the maps are d3, from jsDelivr (allowed by the
     site's script-src). With reduced motion, or under 860px, every scene
     shows its last frame and the page reads straight down.

     Route (Ghost Admin, Labs, Routes):
       /the-faith-received/guide/:
         template: custom-faith-guide --}}

<main class="faith-received tfr-guide-page">
  <div class="tg" data-guide-root data-base="" data-pin-below=".tfr-rail" data-assets="/assets/data/faith-received/guides/">
    <p class="tg-loading">Loading the guide&hellip;</p>
  </div>
</main>
<script src="{{asset "js/page/faith-tfr-rail.js"}}" defer></script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.12.5/dist/gsap.min.js"></script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.12.5/dist/ScrollTrigger.min.js"></script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/d3@7.9.0/dist/d3.min.js"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-guide.js"}}&amp;frv=88e318bdbea00f91"></script>
